<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>arc_recorder</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
    <name>Generated from ARC'26 Manual v.3</name>
    <email>info@anatolianroverchallenge.com</email>
  </author>

  <description>
    Data recorder prop used in the Anatolian Rover Challenge (ARC'26)
    Collaboration Mission, "Sensor Task" (Manual section 7.1.4.1, step 2:
    "Transport the Recorder" -- "Disconnect the cables from the data
    recorder unit at the Sensor Zone, then deliver the device to the
    base. The recorder has a carry handle and uses a USB type-A
    connector.") and referenced in the technical drawing of section 8.6
    "Recorder - Collaboration Mission" (page 48 of the manual).

    The recorder is a free-standing, jerry-can-shaped enclosure with:
      - A rounded rectangular body (300 mm wide footprint)
      - A chamfered top-left corner (in the drawing's side view) where
        the front shoulder transitions to the handle mount
      - An integrated low carry handle molded into the top, with an
        oval grip aperture approx. 90 mm wide
      - A small connector socket/plug (USB type-A, per the mission
        text) mounted on the opposite (right) top shoulder, offset
        approx. 26 mm down from the top reference line
      - A coiled cable running from the connector to the ground
        sensor unit (see the companion "arc_sensor" model), which has
        a stalk diameter of 20 mm and overall length of 148 mm at its
        connector end
      - Total height: 335 mm (to the top of the handle ridge)
      - Height to top of the main body (before the handle mound): 295 mm
      - Footprint width: 300 mm

    All dimensions were taken directly from the dimensioned technical
    drawing in the manual (values in millimetres, converted to metres
    here per SDF convention). The handle aperture and connector are
    secondary features reconstructed proportionally from the drawing's
    illustration, since they were not separately dimensioned beyond
    the 34 mm / 26 mm / 90 mm callouts shown.
  </description>
</model>
